# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPLATE — copy this file, never edit the copy into version control.
#
#   cp config/.env.template config/.env     (or: copy config/.env.template .env)
#
# `config/.env` is gitignored (see .gitignore). This template is safe to commit
# because it contains PLACEHOLDERS ONLY, never a working credential.
#
# ⚠️ WHY ENV VARS ONLY: this project talks to billable real quantum hardware. A
# leaked token is a leaked billable resource tied to a real account. The code
# reads these values with os.getenv() only — never from a file it writes, and
# never from a command-line argument (which would land in the shell history).
#
# The loader is OPTIONAL: python/tkr_ibm.py wraps the `dotenv` import in
# try/except, so the module imports and `--help` works without python-dotenv
# installed. Installing the `dev` extra pulls python-dotenv in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED. IBM Quantum API token.
# Create one at https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com → Account settings → API key.
# The value is shown only once.
IBM_QUANTUM_API_TOKEN=your_api_key_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Cloud Resource Name (CRN) of the instance to use. When unset, the runtime
# picks the instance the token has access to.
# IBM_QUANTUM_INSTANCE=crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:us-east:a/xxxxx::

# Platform channel. Default: ibm_quantum_platform
# IBM_QUANTUM_CHANNEL=ibm_quantum_platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEGACY ALTERNATIVES — either the IBM_QUANTUM_* name above or the QISKIT_IBM_*
# name here is read; the IBM_QUANTUM_* name takes precedence. Provided so the
# code also works in setups that already export the Qiskit-standard variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# QISKIT_IBM_TOKEN=your_api_key_here
# QISKIT_IBM_INSTANCE=crn:v1:bluemix:public:quantum-computing:us-east:a/xxxxx::
